  "body": "## Symptom\n\nOn the Web app (`127.0.0.1:8787`) picking a model in the composer showed a red toast and changed nothing:\n\n```\n\u6a21\u578b\u64cd\u4f5c\u5931\u8d25\uff1aschedule/unavailable: Durable controlled task storage is unavailable\n```\n\nThe models dialog could fetch the endpoint's models (after #9), and the new models were listed in the composer menu \u2014 but selecting one always failed.\n\n## Root cause (two defects, same configuration)\n\nThe Web app runs without `HARNESS_DATA_DIR` unless a launch lease supplies one (`start-web.cmd` does not set it), so `host.dataDir === undefined` and the stores are the memory fakes. In that shape:\n\n1. `apps/web/src/deepseek/activity.ts` \u2014 `state()` refused with `schedule/unavailable` whenever the host owned no durable task file. `draftBlockers()` (reached from `session/selectModel` \u2192 `owners.selectModel` \u2192 `assertDraft` \u2192 `composition.draftBlockers`) treats that refusal as a hard stop, so **every** model change on the memory-only host failed. A read-only \"what is pending\" question must not be fatal when the answer is \"nothing can be pending\".\n2. `packages/harness/src/mem-stores.ts` \u2014 `MemEventStore` stamped sequences with one store-wide counter starting at `1`, while the durable stores (`@ar/events` JSONL, `@ar/store` SQLite) allocate per session from `0`. `assertDraft()` requires a draft journal to be a *dense* prefix (`event.sequence !== index` \u2192 `session/alias-corrupt: A draft journal is not a dense immutable prefix`), which the memory fake could never satisfy.\n\nVerified reproducer before the fix: a fresh memory-only draft had `sequences: [1]` with `nextSequence: 2`.\n\n## Fix\n\n- `activity.ts`: one `durableStorage()` predicate; `state()` keeps refusing (real task mutations are still unavailable), while `sessionActivity()` / `stopSessionActivity()` report zero pending work on a memory-only host and `start()` skips its timer \u2014 the same shape `start()` already used.\n- `mem-stores.ts`: `MemEventStore` allocates per-session, zero-based sequences through a `Map<SessionId, number>`, matching the durable stores' contract.\n- `composition.integration.test.ts`: fixture gained a `durableStorage: false` shape; new case asserts the memory-only host (a) exposes a dense zero-based per-session journal, (b) still changes a draft model through `session/selectModel`, and (c) still refuses `schedule/catalog` with `schedule/unavailable`.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `pnpm typecheck` \u2014 pass.\n- `apps/web/src/deepseek/composition.integration.test.ts` + `packages/harness/src` \u2014 434 passed, 1 skipped (the single failure is the pre-existing `EPERM` symlink case in this environment).\n- Full `pnpm test` \u2014 same 16 environmental failures as the unmodified baseline (symlink privilege + benchmark suites that require a clean committed tree); `catalog.test.ts` and `composition.integration.test.ts` pass.\n- Real app on 8787, after `pnpm build` + restart: settings \u2192 \u6a21\u578b \u2192 \u81ea\u5b9a\u4e49\u6a21\u578b API \u2192 provider `aa` \u2192 \u300c\u83b7\u53d6\u53ef\u7528\u6a21\u578b\u300d listed the endpoint's models, and picking `qmodel` returned\n  `session/selectModel` \u2192 `200 {\"ok\":true,\"value\":{\"selected\":{\"provider\":\"aa\",\"model\":\"qmodel\"}}}` with no failure toast.\n\nScope: only the Web host's task-state guard and the memory event fake. Durable hosts keep their behaviour (they use the SQLite/JSONL stores, which already number per session from 0).\n",
